WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.474
- I'm getting such a
feeling of like ugh from it.

00:00:03.474 --> 00:00:07.125
Like it's the last place
I wanna be right now.

00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:10.375
(creepy playful music)

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:19.328
- So when I was about,
I'd say seven years old

00:00:19.328 --> 00:00:22.811
I went to a birthday party
and they had a bouncy house.

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:24.732
And I'm bouncing around,
having a good time like you do

00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:26.649
when you're a kid in a bouncy house.

00:00:26.649 --> 00:00:29.984
And then at some point I was in a corner

00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:33.236
and then I fell and then
someone near me fell

00:00:33.236 --> 00:00:36.074
and the added weight started to weigh down

00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:37.531
the corner of the bouncy house.

00:00:37.531 --> 00:00:41.972
And I remember feeling some,
this weight on my body.

00:00:41.972 --> 00:00:45.625
- I was about 10 years old and
we were having a family party

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.148
so my mom thought it would be fun

00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:49.485
if she rented a bouncy house.

00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:51.739
So we decided that we
were gonna have some fun

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:53.569
in the bouncy house
before anyone got there.

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:56.189
My dad was leaf-blowing
so he had headphones on

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.143
to block the sound from the leaf blower.

00:00:58.143 --> 00:01:00.869
He accidentally unplugged the bouncy house

00:01:00.869 --> 00:01:03.481
while my mom and my
brothers were inside of it

00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:06.732
and then all of a sudden it
rapidly started deflating.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:10.784
And so my mom took charge
and saved all of our lives.

00:01:10.784 --> 00:01:13.480
- I was probably four years old.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.709
Big birthday party for
a classmate of mine.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.324
I'm sort of off in the
corner, so I kind of

00:01:19.324 --> 00:01:21.584
bounce my way over, there's a kid

00:01:21.584 --> 00:01:24.817
with one of the balls from the ball pit.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.236
He's using the ball to wipe his ass.

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:28.785
And so, really ever since then

00:01:28.785 --> 00:01:30.555
I've been a little bit traumatized.

00:01:30.555 --> 00:01:33.777
- And I distinctly remember feeling like

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:37.388
"Oh my God, life is real and
there is pain in the world

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:39.493
"and I'm experiencing it right now."

00:01:39.493 --> 00:01:41.692
Like genuine terror and fear.

00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:43.411
- So ever since then I have been

00:01:43.411 --> 00:01:45.340
quite fearful of bouncy houses.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.303
- I mean, I just think that kids

00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:49.468
do disgusting things in these things.

00:01:49.468 --> 00:01:52.551
(funky upbeat music)

00:01:54.764 --> 00:01:58.440
- No, I'm not going into a bounce house.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.558
- (laughing) No.

00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:01.128
- You know, I'm sure I could handle it.

00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:03.649
Why, do you guys have a bounce house?

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:04.482
- You do?

00:02:04.482 --> 00:02:06.475
- There's a bouncy house here?

00:02:06.475 --> 00:02:07.535
Oh my God.

00:02:07.535 --> 00:02:08.368
- Oh no.

00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:11.250
- I can hear it.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.936
- I'm actually gonna bounce
in a bouncy house today.

00:02:13.936 --> 00:02:15.544
- Hello, old friend.

00:02:15.544 --> 00:02:16.544
- Oh my God!

00:02:18.225 --> 00:02:20.881
How did I not know this
was gonna be a thing?

00:02:20.881 --> 00:02:23.740
- I'm getting such a
feeling of like ugh from it.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.009
Like it's the last place
I wanna be right now.

00:02:27.009 --> 00:02:28.943
- You think I could make it through there?

00:02:28.943 --> 00:02:31.193
(laughter)

00:02:32.836 --> 00:02:35.332
- It's not that I dislike bounce houses

00:02:35.332 --> 00:02:38.288
I'm realizing that I think
I might be afraid of them.

00:02:38.288 --> 00:02:39.503
- You know, it's not that upsetting.

00:02:39.503 --> 00:02:42.480
It's very, it's bouncy but you know

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.875
my head's right here, I got a giant head.

00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:47.229
(suspenseful music)
- Alright.

00:02:47.229 --> 00:02:49.844
- You can put this in black
and white, dramatic recreation.

00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:53.832
I fell and then the next
kid fell on me and then

00:02:53.832 --> 00:02:58.111
they all piled on and I
was crushed in such a way.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.630
- This is a blast, I feel like
I'm reliving my childhood.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.713
- No, no I don't like it.

00:03:05.304 --> 00:03:07.675
(laughing)

00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:09.076
- Ooh yeah, you see that?

00:03:09.076 --> 00:03:12.088
- Maybe it has nothing
to do with the incident.

00:03:12.088 --> 00:03:15.067
Maybe I just deep down hate bounce houses.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:17.577
I now have two traumatic
bounce house stories.

00:03:17.577 --> 00:03:19.361
- You know, I'm not afraid, I acknowledge

00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:21.587
that what happened was an
accident when I was a kid

00:03:21.587 --> 00:03:25.588
and I'm not, you know, there's
nothing to be afraid of.

00:03:25.588 --> 00:03:26.958
(laughs) Good bit.

00:03:26.958 --> 00:03:28.919
- (laughing) Oh my God!

00:03:28.919 --> 00:03:31.763
You guys, I can't believe you did this.

00:03:31.763 --> 00:03:34.013
This is epic, props, props.

00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:39.475
(groovy music)

